# OpenAI API key — writes the Somali reel script and generates the bespoke
# scene visuals. Without it, scripts fall back to the canned offline templates
# (which are about a fixed set of subjects, NOT the topic you asked for) and
# scenes fall back to stock photography or the offline poster card.
# Get a key at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys — note that a ChatGPT
# subscription does NOT include API access; the API is billed separately.
# Roughly $0.04 per six-scene reel at the defaults below.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the OpenAI image model. Defaults to gpt-image-1-mini,
# the cheapest (~$0.006/image at low quality).
# OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1-mini

# Optional: OpenAI image quality — low (default), medium, or high. Raising it
# increases cost per image sharply; low is usually enough because the render
# is downscaled into a 1080x1920 frame anyway.
# OPENAI_IMAGE_QUALITY=low

# Optional: override the OpenAI model used for script writing.
# Defaults to gpt-5.4-mini.
# OPENAI_SCRIPT_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini

# Pexels API key — free stock photography, used for scene visuals whenever
# OpenAI cannot produce an image (no key, or out of credit). Free for
# commercial use, 200 requests/hour and 20,000 per month, which is roughly
# 3,300 six-scene reels. Get a key in two minutes, no card, at
# https://www.pexels.com/api/ . Without it, those scenes fall back to the
# offline Xeero poster card instead of a real photograph.
PEXELS_API_KEY=
